- [Run 1 terminal screenshot](</home/james/rung3-chung-cu/R3-074/2026-11-26T20-42-43+07-00-run1-terminal.png>) and [run 2 terminal screenshot](</home/james/rung3-chung-cu/R3-074/2026-11-26T20-44-02+07-00-run2-terminal.png>)
- [Fixed script copy](</home/james/rung3-chung-cu/R3-074/d40-tinh-toan.py>), [run 1 result](</home/james/rung3-chung-cu/R3-074/ket-qua-run1.txt>), and [run 2 result](</home/james/rung3-chung-cu/R3-074/ket-qua-run2.txt>)
- [Report](</home/james/rung3-chung-cu/R3-074/bao-cao.txt>), [full drive log with anomaly chains](</home/james/rung3-chung-cu/R3-074/drive-log.txt>), [start time](</home/james/rung3-chung-cu/R3-074/start_time.txt>), and [end time](</home/james/rung3-chung-cu/R3-074/end_time.txt>)
- [Pill visible during the drive](</home/james/rung3-chung-cu/R3-074/pill-during-drive.png>) and [desktop after release](</home/james/rung3-chung-cu/R3-074/desktop-after-pill-release.png>)

**Pill times:** Session 1 acquired 20:29:55 and exited unexpectedly at 20:31:22; session 2 acquired 20:31:49 and was cleanly released at 20:46:18. The 20:46:26 screenshot confirms the pill was gone.

**Anomalies and outcomes:**

- A read-only window-list command had a Python quoting error → I identified it as a diagnostic formatting issue → simplified and reran the query → preflight remained clear.
- `Ctrl+Alt+T` did not open a terminal, and a Super-only action was refused before input → I tried `Super+Space` → used `Super+Return` → Kitty opened on workspace 2.
- The first driver exited while observing Kitty → I checked session and desktop state without killing it → started a fresh driver → continued with the existing Kitty window.
- The “text editor” search selected a setup action that opened a sudo prompt → I entered no credentials; Escape and Alt+F4 did not close it → Ctrl+C, then Alt+F4 on the focused task-created window → prompt closed; searching for and clicking “Visual Studio Code — Text Editor” opened the editor.
- The editor file picker stayed in `/tmp` after Ctrl+L and the path entry → I navigated Home → `rung3` and searched for the filename → opened the exact script.
- “Visual Studio” appeared as unsubmitted Kitty prompt text → I checked it before execution → Ctrl+U cleared it → only the intended script command was submitted.
- Alt+F4 did not close Kitty → I focused the task-created shell and used Ctrl+D → Kitty closed. I closed the script tab in VS Code and left its pre-existing unsaved tab intact.

The fixed script and result file remain in place; the fixture was not reset.
